WEBVTT

00:00:02.600 --> 00:00:04.700
Start in the admin

00:00:04.700 --> 00:00:06.800
The Switch opens

00:00:06.800 --> 00:00:08.500
Providers: women-owned service businesses, verified like brands

00:00:08.500 --> 00:00:10.600
Add provider starts with Step 0 · Check her too

00:00:10.600 --> 00:00:12.700
Clicked into Business name

00:00:12.700 --> 00:00:14.300
Typed the business name

00:00:14.300 --> 00:00:15.700
Clicked into City

00:00:15.700 --> 00:00:17.400
Typed her city

00:00:17.400 --> 00:00:19.000
Chose her state: Colorado — it tells her apart from others with the same name

00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:20.000
Chose the kind of service (optional here) — or “+ New kind…”

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:24.400
Her website, if she has one. Without it, one small search finds it by name and city

00:00:24.400 --> 00:00:29.300
The duplicate check, then the Screen

00:00:29.300 --> 00:00:33.500
Likely women-owned — unlocked. You still confirm her ownership

00:00:33.500 --> 00:00:35.300
The provider form opens on her hidden draft, filled in from the check

00:00:35.300 --> 00:00:39.800
Name, kind, city and state, her site and the evidence came from the check

00:00:39.800 --> 00:00:43.200
Clicked into What she does

00:00:43.200 --> 00:00:44.800
Typed her specialties, comma-separated

00:00:44.800 --> 00:00:49.000
Clicked into Her story

00:00:49.000 --> 00:00:50.800
Her story — only what she wrote or approved

00:00:50.800 --> 00:00:51.700
Ownership: admin-only, and needed to publish

00:00:51.700 --> 00:00:55.900
Published stays off until everything is in — the line under it says what's missing

00:00:55.900 --> 00:00:57.300
Clicked into Owner's full name

00:00:57.300 --> 00:00:59.100
Typed the owner's full name

00:00:59.100 --> 00:01:00.500
Verified on: the day you checked

00:01:00.500 --> 00:01:03.100
The evidence link came from the check

00:01:03.100 --> 00:01:06.500
Published can be ticked now: every requirement is met

00:01:06.500 --> 00:01:08.700
Ticked Published

00:01:08.700 --> 00:01:11.700
Saved

00:01:11.700 --> 00:01:12.800
The list, with the new provider

00:01:12.800 --> 00:01:18.240
The new provider is in the list. In this demo, nothing really went live
